Below is a concise representation of the DNS record descriptors for **`site.info`**.  
I’ve wrapped the information under the key `apikey_info` as requested, and omitted any extraneous attributes—only the essential descriptors (`type`, `ttl`, `data`) are shown.

```json
{
  "apikey_info": {
    "domain": "site.info",
    "records": [
      {
        "type": "A",
        "ttl": 3600,
        "data": "93.184.216.34"
      },
      {
        "type": "AAAA",
        "ttl": 3600,
        "data": "2606:2800:220:1:248:1893:25c8:1946"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

> **Note:**  
> - The IP addresses above are illustrative; actual values may differ depending on your DNS provider and propagation status.  
> - If you need real-time lookups, run `dig site.info +noall +answer` (or `nslookup site.info`) on your terminal.
